#edb/ref 1079 #uuid "412474d7-c770-5c0d-8c2c-215a6bc5fac2" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186558446 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186557921 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186558446 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186557940 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186558446 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186558209 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186558446 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186558301 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186558446 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186558347 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186558446 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186558446 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186558446 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186558301 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186558446 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "b80b6de0-d629-5831-8a5c-74da1f4dac9c" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186558510 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186558373 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186558510 #edb/ref 1069 "q-62052" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186558510 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186558510 #edb/ref 1071 "Austin's average monthly profit has been decreasing at a rate of $6%$ every year. If he initially recorded an average monthly profit of $$58\\,000$, then which function correctly represents $p(t),$ Austin's average monthly profit since the start of the decline?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186558510 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "476bf309-f448-501a-8dca-89cb923e9fd5" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186558510 #edb/ref 1074 "The formula for exponential decay (in terms of a decay rate $r$) is\n\n$$\np(t)=a(1-r)^{t}.\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have the following:\n\n- $a=58\\,000$ is the initial average monthly profit.\n\n- $r=0.06$ is the decay rate ($6%$ expressed as a decimal).\n\n- $t=$ the time, in years.\n\nTherefore, the correct expression for $p$ is\n\n$$\np(t)=58\\,000\\cdot (1-0.06)^{t}=58\\,000\\cdot (0.94)^{t}.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186558525 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186558384 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186558525 #edb/ref 1069 "q-1418" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186558525 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186558525 #edb/ref 1071 "An adult drinks a cup of coffee that contains $110$ mg of caffeine, and each hour the amount of caffeine in their body decreases by $15%.$ To the nearest integer, how much caffeine will be left in their system after $11$ hours?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186558525 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "6c8488d4-9154-55d8-8e4c-cbf91ba1e38c" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186558525 #edb/ref 1074 "The formula for exponential decay (in terms of a decay rate $r$) is\n\n$$\ny=a(1-r)^{t}.\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have the following:\n\n- $a=110$ is the initial amount of caffeine in the adult's body.\n\n- $r=0.15$ is the decay rate ($15%$ expressed as a decimal).\n\n- $t=$ the time, in hours.\n\nTherefore, the correct expression for $y$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =110\\cdot (1-0.15)^{t} \\\\  & =110\\cdot (0.85)^{t}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEvaluating the expression for $t=11$ hours, we get\n\n$$\ny(11)=110\\cdot (0.85)^{11}≈18.\n$$\n\nHence, after $11$ hours, there will be $18$ mg of caffeine left in their system." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186558533 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186558446 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186558533 #edb/ref 1069 "q-62061" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186558533 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186558533 #edb/ref 1071 "A lake currently has a depth of $320$ feet. The depth of the lake is expected to decrease by one-tenth every year.\n\nThe function $d(t)$ models the depth of the lake after $t$ years and is given by\n\n$$\nd(t)=320\\cdot {(\\text{___})}^{t}.\n$$\n\nWhat number is missing?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186558533 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "85b49133-7772-5722-8e3e-dbe769864a2c" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186558533 #edb/ref 1074 "If the depth reduces by $\\frac{1}{10}$ every month, then $\\frac{9}{10}$ of the depth remains every year. So the decay factor is $\\frac{9}{10}.$\n\nThe formula for exponential decay (in terms of a decay factor $b$) is\n\n$$\nd(t)=a{b}^{t}.\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have the following:\n\n- $a=320$ is the initial depth.\n\n- $b=\\frac{9}{10}$ is the decay factor.\n\n- $t=$ the time, in years.\n\nTherefore, the correct expression for $d(t)$ is\n\n$$\nd(t)=320\\cdot {(\\frac{9}{10})}^{t}.\n$$\n\nSo the missing number is $\\frac{9}{10}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186558605 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186558618 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186558605 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "2f1bf5b6-2615-592e-aedc-3e9f1565ab81" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186558605 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186558510 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186558618 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "4812dcec-6a52-59bd-bb5b-c5e1a060a776" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186558618 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186558533 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186558659 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186558605 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186558659 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "9459a6e5-4631-59b7-af40-bc1c6ff0d9df" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186558659 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186558525 #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
